MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1625177508}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3ff6acaa8b9f1994499dd387e6188532, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Comments: This scene demonstrates how to use Video Player with Timeflow. When objects
    with a Video Player component are added to Timeflow, a Video Player Update component
    is automatically added to handle timing updates. This allows videos to be sequenced
    with optional looping and time offsets.
  Warning: 'Enter play mode for video playback.


    Performance and accuracy of
    video playback depends on the video file format and Unity''s implementation of
    video. Timeflow does not perform any video processing or decoding and only sends
    timing updates to Video Player. Frame accuracy or perfect synchronization cannot
    be guaranteed.


    Since video files cannot be included with Asset Store packages,
    please download this test video file linked below, or use one of your own videos.'
  URLTitle: Download Example Video
  URL: https://www.dropbox.com/s/7xyjkl3mqrbihy1/TestVideo.mp4?dl=0
  URL2Title: Video Player Update Documentation
  URL2: https://axongenesis.gitbook.io/timeflow/reference/behaviors/tools/video-player-update
